{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01558",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 6.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.21,
      "end_seconds": 10.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.6,
      "end_seconds": 17.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Good morning, um, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.82,
      "end_seconds": 22.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.22,
      "end_seconds": 29.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Doctor, it's a temperature. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.28,
      "end_seconds": 39.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.92,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.99,
      "end_seconds": 52.28,
      "duration_seconds": 12.29,
      "text": "I, I take alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week. It's metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 53.75,
      "end_seconds": 66.66,
      "duration_seconds": 12.91,
      "text": "Um, um, doctor, I think the last prescription for the metoprolol was 100 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.68,
      "end_seconds": 72.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.71,
      "end_seconds": 95.06,
      "duration_seconds": 20.35,
      "text": "Um, no, I left it at home. Tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night for the prostate. So, I take paracetamol syrup, 5 ml, every six hours. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.99,
      "end_seconds": 99.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "So, and for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.14,
      "end_seconds": 103.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "For about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.89,
      "end_seconds": 112.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Alright, how long has it been like this? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.57,
      "end_seconds": 120.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Oh, I'd say about a week. Actually, no, closer to about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.68,
      "end_seconds": 125.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Alright, how often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.83,
      "end_seconds": 149.94,
      "duration_seconds": 23.11,
      "text": "I'd say on and off. And there's ear pain as well, uh, about four days now. Okay, um, so with ear pain, it's worse with lying down. Let me think, I've had not eating too, for one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.37,
      "end_seconds": 153.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "How about stiff neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.93,
      "end_seconds": 157.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "No. No stiff neck."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.63,
      "end_seconds": 164.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Have you had any discharge, swelling behind the ear or hearing loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.61,
      "end_seconds": 177.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "Actually, I haven't had discharge, swelling behind the ear or hearing loss, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.43,
      "end_seconds": 183.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.1,
      "end_seconds": 186.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.38,
      "end_seconds": 200.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.38,
      "end_seconds": 203.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.84,
      "end_seconds": 205.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.31,
      "end_seconds": 209.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.51,
      "end_seconds": 213.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.07,
      "end_seconds": 219.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.67,
      "end_seconds": 223.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "So, do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.48,
      "end_seconds": 226.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.85,
      "end_seconds": 248.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.31,
      "end_seconds": 256.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Erm, my aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.97,
      "end_seconds": 274.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.4,
      "end_seconds": 282.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Yes, uh, I had a meniscus repair on my knee, four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.49,
      "end_seconds": 288.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.41,
      "end_seconds": 296.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "Ah, you know, I've had thin bones for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.88,
      "end_seconds": 298.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.8,
      "end_seconds": 305.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.56,
      "end_seconds": 307.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.61,
      "end_seconds": 316.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, yes, an enlarged prostate. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.33,
      "end_seconds": 324.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Understood. Alright, thin bones and an enlarged prostate, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 329.38,
      "end_seconds": 337.03,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pressure 106 over 66, saturation 97 percent, temperature 39.0, pulse 98."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.0,
      "end_seconds": 339.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.3,
      "end_seconds": 347.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.82,
      "end_seconds": 350.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Yeah, um, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.21,
      "end_seconds": 353.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.81,
      "end_seconds": 372.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "The right ear drum is red and bulging, and the left is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.93,
      "end_seconds": 386.99,
      "duration_seconds": 12.06,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Okay, so my impression is this: I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at acute middle ear infection or a viral cold."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.13,
      "end_seconds": 391.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.38,
      "end_seconds": 428.0,
      "duration_seconds": 34.62,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like acute middle ear infection. The treatment will be amoxicillin, 250 milligrams, three times a day, five days. That should help with ear infection. Give pain relief regularly and plenty to drink. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.71,
      "end_seconds": 433.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Ah, no, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}